Q: Looping SVG as an &lt;hr /&gt; graphic A: <p>Define a <strong>browser native</strong> Web Component <code>&lt;svg-rope&gt;</code><br />
that <strong>repeats</strong> your rope-shape-segments inside a <em>new</em> SVG.</p>
<p>Usage is the same in bare HTML or any Frame(d)work</p>
<pre><code>&lt;svg-rope&gt;&lt;/svg-rope&gt;
&lt;svg-rope color=&quot;grey&quot;&gt;&lt;/svg-rope&gt;
</code></pre>
<p><img src="https://i.sstatic.net/M6cdTB6p.png" alt="enter image description here" /></p>
<p>I added some extra config examples because just the bare <code>&lt;svg-rope&gt;</code> Web Component was too simple.</p>
<p>Change the <code>rope</code> d-path to make it look <em>less</em> like a boring straight rope</p>
<p>Change the <code>dur=&quot;.5&quot;</code> to display the rope faster or slower</p>
<p>Note I put the SVG inside shadowDOM, so all styles <em>inside</em> are safeguarded.<br />
The standard CSS <code>::part</code> pseudo-selector <strong>can</strong> style elements  inside shadowDOM.<br />
If you do want to style <em>everything</em> with <em>global CSS</em> just remove the <code>.attachShadow</code> call.</p>
<p>Code is also available at: <a href="https://jsfiddle.net/WebComponents/weL9p572/" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://jsfiddle.net/WebComponents/weL9p572/</a></p>
<p>Have fun!</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;script&gt;
  customElements.define("svg-rope", class extends HTMLElement {
    connectedCallback() {
      let count = 14; // segment count
      let width = 600;
      let rope = `&lt;path id="rope" fill="none" stroke="brown" d="m0 25h${count*40}"/&gt;`;
      let shape = `m0,-15c5.21,-7 25.61,-8.79 37.72,0.1l42.6,31.17c-5.21,7-25.61,8.79-37.72,-0.1z`;
      let color = this.getAttribute("color") || "burlywood";
      let segment = (point,idx) =&gt; 
          `&lt;path d="${shape}" part="segment segment-${idx}" fill="${color}"&gt;` +
          ` &lt;animateMotion dur=".5s" fill="freeze" keyPoints="0;${point}" keyTimes="0;1" calcMode="linear"&gt;` +
          `  &lt;mpath href="#rope"/&gt;` +
          ` &lt;/animateMotion&gt;` +
          `&lt;/path&gt;`;
      let segments = Array.from({ length: count-1 }, (_, idx) =&gt; segment(idx / (count - 1), idx));
      let svg = `&lt;svg part="svg" viewBox="0 0 ${width} 50"&gt;${segments.join('')}${rope}&lt;/svg&gt;`;
      this.attachShadow({mode:"open"})
          .innerHTML = "&lt;style&gt;:host{display:block}&lt;/style&gt;" + svg;
    }
  });
&lt;/script&gt;
&lt;style&gt;
  svg-rope::part(svg) {
    background:pink;
  }
  svg-rope::part(segment) {
    stroke: black;
  }
  svg-rope::part(segment-1) {
    fill:red;
  }
&lt;/style&gt;
&lt;svg-rope&gt;&lt;/svg-rope&gt;
&lt;svg-rope color="grey"&gt;&lt;/svg-rope&gt;
&lt;svg-rope color="hotpink"&gt;&lt;/svg-rope&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>
<p>!IMPORTANT
Unlike Frame(d)works and jQuery and HTMX or anything else, it totally does <strong>not</strong> matter <em>when</em> you execute this script, can be in the <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> , <code>&lt;body&gt;</code> or executed 5 minutes later.<br />
Every <code>&lt;svg-rope&gt;</code> <strong>in</strong> the page is <em>automagically</em> created.<br />
Because Web Components <strong><em>are</em></strong> HTML, and all other technologies <strong><em>create</em></strong> HTML</p>
